# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- virtualenvs --------------------------------------------------------------
# `.venv` is 17 runtime packages plus 11 dev packages. It is rebuilt from
# requirements*.txt in about 30 seconds and it pins nothing the pins do not
# already pin, so it has no business in the history. F-15: gunicorn is marked
# `sys_platform != "win32"`, so a Windows venv is NOT the container's
# dependency set. Never debug against it instead of the image.
.venv/
venv/

# --- runtime state ------------------------------------------------------------
# The instance volume is a named Docker volume, but a local run (tests,
# manage.py) leaves a file behind. SQLite databases are generated.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
data/instance/
data/media/
src/media/
staticfiles/

# --- secret material ----------------------------------------------------------
# Keys live on their own volume and must never enter the repository. If a key
# is ever committed the signed records it produced are forgeable and every
# record has to be reissued. There is no recovery path; do not add an exception
# to this line.
*.pem
*.key
keys/

# --- local acceptance ---------------------------------------------------------
# `.dogfood.toml` holds the seed session cookies, which are printed by the
# container on boot. They are already public in spec.md, so this is habit
# rather than secrecy -- but a config that names our own base_url does not
# belong in history either.
.env
.env.*

# --- the planning layer ------------------------------------------------------
# NOT part of the product, and deliberately not published.
#
# `bible/` is 400 KB of competition research (mission and win conditions,
# requirements traceability, an hour-by-hour delivery plan). `blueprint/` is the
# build plan, the 126-entry findings ledger and fourteen feature archives.
# `AGENTS.md` is the operating instructions for an AI agent working in this
# folder, and the two files at the root were scratch notes addressed to one.
#
# None of it is what this repository is for. A repository whose subject is a
# judging platform should open on the judging platform. Git history keeps all of
# it -- `git show HEAD~1:blueprint/context/findings.md` -- so nothing is lost, it
# is only no longer the front door.
#
# The consequence is handled rather than ignored: `tools/verify_spec.py` and
# `tests/test_schema_contract.py` read these files, and both now SKIP the checks
# whose subject is absent instead of failing on a clone that has never seen it.
AGENTS.md
HANDOFF.md
context.txt
bible/
blueprint/

# --- editors and OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
